        <briefdescription>
<para>Encodes a vector of uint8_t into a Node object. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function takes an input vector of uint8_t and encodes it into a Node object by assigning each element of the vector to a corresponding index in the Node object. The encoding is done using a for loop, where each element from the input vector is assigned to a position in the Node object.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>rhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A const reference to an std::vector&lt;uint8_t&gt; that needs to be encoded into a Node object. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Returns a Node object which contains the encoded data from the input vector. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
